.TH WHATERMAK 1 "July 2026" "whatermak 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whatermak \- display a click-through image watermark on Sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whatermak
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIIMAGE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whatermak
displays a transparent image on a Wayland layer of every output. It uses the
layer-shell protocol, reserves no screen space, and accepts no pointer or
keyboard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIOUTPUT\fR
Show only on an output index or exact monitor name.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-primary
Show only on the primary output.
.TP
.BR \-\-position =\fIPOSITION\fR
One of top-left, top, top-right, left, center, right, bottom-left, bottom, or
bottom-right. The default is bottom-right.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-layer =\fILAYER\fR
One of background, bottom, top, or overlay. Bottom places the watermark above
the wallpaper but below normal windows. The default is overlay.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width =\fIPIXELS\fR
Rendered width in logical pixels. The default is 240.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-margin =\fIPIXELS\fR
Distance from anchored edges. The default is 32.
.TP
.BR \-\-opacity =\fIVALUE\fR
Opacity greater than 0.0 and at most 1.0. The default is 0.22.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
whatermak ~/Pictures/company.png
whatermak --layer=bottom watermark.png
whatermak --position=center --width=480 --opacity=0.12 watermark.png
whatermak --output=1 watermark.png
.fi
